anna (APIs): Quick heads-up — I'm rolling a pragmatic response-shape change for /v2/generate. PR up: https://github.com/redwood-inference/platform/pull/1234. Goal: add explicit schema/version hints so SDKs can opt-in and we can keep a one-release compatibility layer.

mike (sdk): Quick Q — how will the SDK treat the old top-level 'choices' when the new 'output' object exists? currently missing -> undefined and our strict parsers throw.

jess (runtime): We should not break. Plan: if client requests v2 (via Accept header or vendor media type) we return the new structured shape. Otherwise we include a compat wrapper that keeps 'choices' present. Runtime will set Content-Type and an X-RW-Schema header for clarity.

anna (APIs): Prefer content-negotiation: `Accept: application/vnd.redwood+json; version=2`. Avoid inventing ad-hoc query params. We will also add `X-RW-Schema: 2` as a response hint for debugging.

mike (sdk): For streaming clients (ndjson) can we emit a schema announce line at the start so parsers know what to expect?

jess (runtime): Yes. For streaming we plan to emit a single-line schema marker as the first NDJSON chunk, e.g.:

```json
{"schema":"2","type":"schema-announce"}
```

After that we stream the usual event chunks (token / delta / done). For non-streaming, Content-Type will be `application/vnd.redwood+json; version=2` or the compat `application/json`.

anna (APIs): Example response shape (non-streaming) for v2 with compat shim:

```json
{
  "schema_version": "2",
  "output": {
    "choices": [
      {"id":"c1","text_chunks": ["hi"], "structured": {"intent":"answer"}}
    ],
    "metadata": {"model":"rwd-4b"}
  },
  "deprecated_choices": [
    {"text":"hi","index":0}
  ]
}
```

jess (runtime): Implementation notes: runtime will populate `deprecated_choices` from the new `output.choices` when the client did NOT signal v2. That keeps existing clients happy while v2 consumers can rely on richer shape. We'll add a config toggle so Dedicated customers can opt into strict mode earlier.

mike (sdk): I'll land an SDK patch to prefer `output` when present, but fall back to `deprecated_choices` for one release. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/5678. Will add unit tests with the NDJSON announce + compat stream fixture.

anna (APIs): Tests + canary plan: add contract tests under `/tests/contracts/v2/compat/` and run canary in us-west1 tonight (small %). cc @deploy-bot

deploy-bot: Canary deploy started for v2-schema-compat at 2026-03-17T02:15Z :rocket:

mike (sdk): Noted. I'll add test vectors and a changelog entry calling out the compat layer.

jess (runtime): Also adding an internal smoke-check that validates Content-Type and X-RW-Schema are set correctly for both streaming and non-streaming.

anna (APIs): Great. Action items: mike - sdk patch + tests; jess - runtime toggle + smoke checks; me - docs + PR for media type and changelog. We'll remove `deprecated_choices` in the next major. Marking this thread resolved unless blockers appear. Thanks all :thumbsup:
